@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Security Best Practices";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Security in DevOps is essential to protect infrastructure, applications, and data from threats. Following security best practices ensures compliance, resilience, and a robust development lifecycle.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Why is Security Important in DevOps?</h2>
        <p>Security in DevOps, often called DevSecOps, integrates security into the development lifecycle. Key benefits include:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Early Vulnerability Detection:</strong> Identifies security risks during development.</li>
            <li><strong>Compliance & Governance:</strong> Ensures adherence to security policies and regulatory standards.</li>
            <li><strong>Automated Threat Mitigation:</strong> Uses CI/CD security checks to prevent vulnerabilities.</li>
            <li><strong>Least Privilege Access Control:</strong> Limits exposure by granting only necessary permissions.</li>
            <li><strong>Continuous Monitoring:</strong> Uses logging and analytics for real-time security insights.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/security/media/security-best-practices.png" alt="DevSecOps Security Best Practices" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
        <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Security best practices in DevSecOps</small></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Key Security Best Practices</h2>
        <p>To build a secure DevOps pipeline, teams should follow these security principles:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Use Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA):</strong> Protect user accounts with additional security layers.</li>
            <li><strong>Implement Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):</strong> Restrict access based on job responsibilities.</li>
            <li><strong>Secure Code Repositories:</strong> Enforce branch protection, code reviews, and security scanning.</li>
            <li><strong>Encrypt Sensitive Data:</strong> Use Azure Key Vault to store secrets and encryption keys.</li>
            <li><strong>Scan Dependencies for Vulnerabilities:</strong> Automate security scans for third-party packages.</li>
            <li><strong>Enforce Secure CI/CD Pipelines:</strong> Implement security gates and compliance checks.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Security in CI/CD Pipelines</h3>
        <p>DevOps teams must integrate security checks within their CI/CD pipelines. Key steps include:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Code Scanning:</strong> Use tools like SonarQube, GitHub Advanced Security, or WhiteSource.</li>
            <li><strong>Secrets Management:</strong> Store credentials securely using Azure Key Vault.</li>
            <li><strong>Container Security:</strong> Scan Docker images for vulnerabilities before deployment.</li>
            <li><strong>Infrastructure as Code (IaC) Security:</strong> Use policy-as-code to enforce security guidelines.</li>
            <li><strong>Security Testing:</strong> Automate penetration testing and fuzz testing in CI/CD pipelines.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Example YAML for Secure CI/CD Pipeline</h3>
        <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
steps:
- task: WhiteSource@21
  inputs:
    organizationServiceConnection: 'MyAzureConnection'
    scanType: 'Full'
    failBuildOnPolicyViolation: true
        </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Best Practices for Ongoing Security</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Regularly Update Dependencies:</strong> Patch vulnerabilities by keeping libraries up to date.</li>
            <li><strong>Monitor Logs & Alerts:</strong> Use Azure Security Center for real-time threat detection.</li>
            <li><strong>Zero Trust Architecture:</strong> Verify every access request regardless of network location.</li>
            <li><strong>Apply Least Privilege Access:</strong> Restrict administrative privileges to reduce risk.</li>
            <li><strong>Conduct Security Audits:</strong> Regularly review access policies and security configurations.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>Security best practices in DevOps protect infrastructure, applications, and sensitive data from cyber threats. By embedding security into CI/CD workflows, teams can maintain compliance and prevent breaches.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-end mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("RBAC", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>